# brainstorm-toolkit cheatsheet

Printable one-pager. Lives at the repo root after `setup.sh` runs. Edit
freely — `setup.sh` skips this file once it exists, so your customizations
survive plugin upgrades.

For the **always-current** view of installed skills, run `README.md` —
it reads the SKILL.md frontmatter directly and never goes stale. This file
is the *map*; `README.md` is the *menu*.

---

## Pipeline at a glance

```
                ┌─────────────────────────┐
                │       /brainstorm       │  ← idea, no plan yet
                └────────────┬────────────┘
                             ▼
                  plans/brainstorm-*.md
                             │
              ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
              ▼                             ▼
       /sdlc {plan}                    /task "..."
       /sdlc-lite <X>                  (single-row TDD)
              │                             │
              ▼                             ▼
   sanity → implement → evals → fix         inline TDD
   → validate
   → [review → review-fix]  (opt-in)
              │                             │
        ┌─────┴─────┐                       │
        ▼           ▼                       │
   /sdlc: PR    /sdlc-lite:                 │
                validated tree ─────────────┘
                (you commit)
                      │
                   merged
                      │
                      ▼
```

Back-edges — how a stalled or landed run re-enters:

```
  run paused/failed  → /status  → drafted fix → /sdlc-lite <X> --resume
  "where was I?"     → /status             → reads envelope + sentinel + TASKS.md
```

Execution tiers — same pipeline in the middle, different ending:

```
  /task "..."       → TDD red→green only. Commits only if you ask.
                      Fast path for a one-liner, util, or rename.
  /sdlc-lite <X>    → FULL pipeline, then HANDS YOU the validated changes
                      to commit. No git writes.
                      <X> = plan file | task-id | range "1-5" | description
                            | --queue [N] (attended backlog loop)
  /sdlc {plan}      → FULL pipeline, then commits → branch → push → PR.
                      The only tier that touches git history.

  Stage 2 (implement) auto-decomposes a large multi-surface plan (>=2
  disjoint surfaces, >=6 steps) into focused per-lane subagents + a
  converge step; small / single-surface plans run one agent. No flag —
  the gate is automatic. Threshold: agents.decompose_min_tasks (default 6).
```

Cost control — two INDEPENDENT model axes. Keep them straight:

```
  AXIS 1 — the fan-out ladder (haiku < sonnet < opus). A CEILING.
    project.json → "models": { "cap": "sonnet" }   (standing policy)
    per run:       /sdlc-lite {plan} --model sonnet
                   (precedence: flag > config > built-in default)

    The cap only ever LOWERS: Opus dispatches drop to it; Haiku is NOT
    upgraded. Per-stage defaults live in models.sanity / .plan_review /
    .implement — those are the ONLY way to RAISE a Haiku stage.
    Governs sub-agents only — for full savings also set your session model.

    DEFAULT is Sonnet-first: /sdlc, /sdlc-lite, /brainstorm --vet and the
    ultracode workflows run Sonnet out of the box; --model opus opts up.

  AXIS 2 — the adversarial reviewer (Stage 5.7/5.8 only). NEVER capped.
    "models": { "code_review": "opus" }  or  --review-model <name>
    Accepts fable, which is NOT a rung on the ladder. Opt-in permanently:
    the stage never runs unless explicitly enabled.

  Reviewer/agent COUNTS are a separate block:
    "agents": { "code_review_lenses": [...], "code_review_passes": 1,
                "sanity_focuses": [...] }   ← cost scales ~linearly

  Full contract: skills/sdlc/templates/models.md
```

In parallel, runnable any time:

```
  /status             → "what should I do now?" — the canonical next-step ladder
  /status           → current pipeline run state at a glance
  /repo-health      → scored sweep, prints the highest-impact next command
  /status  → classify a paused run → drafted fix → --resume re-entry
  /dead-code-review → deeper, multi-agent unused-code scan
  /flowsim {plan}   → trace claimed flows through code, flag drift
  /test-check       → run tests + log audit
  /test-check --loop → browser/E2E tests in a bounded fix loop
  /eval-harness     → scaffold + run the eval suite
  /plan-html {plan} → render any markdown plan as a single-file shareable HTML
  /gotcha "<entry>" → capture a pitfall (also auto-drafted at loop-exit by
                      /task, /sdlc, /sdlc-lite on real traps; injected at
                      /brainstorm start)
```

Ideation family — pick by ambiguity, not by topic:

```
  /brainstorm [topic]      → fast conversational, low ambiguity
  /brainstorm-deep [topic] → clarification-heavy (3-pass + perspective frames
                             + expectation contract) for ambiguous / high-stakes
  /brainstorm-team [topic] → multi-agent product/competitive research team
```

