## Install / refresh

| Route | Command | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| Plugin | `/plugin marketplace add <repo>` then `/plugin install brainstorm-toolkit` | Claude Code, all repos |
| `setup.sh` | `bash <plugin>/setup.sh --target . --tools all` | this repo (Claude + Copilot + Codex) |
| Global | `bash <plugin>/scripts/sync-global.sh` | `~/.claude/`, no plugin registration |

`--tools` takes `claude` \| `copilot` \| `codex` \| `both` \| `all`. Re-run
`setup.sh` any time; it skips existing files unless you pass `--force`, and
never overwrites `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / `TASKS.md` / `project.json`.
Use `sync-global.sh` when the plugin route is blocked (e.g. an org policy
setting `disableSideloadFlags`); don't run it *and* the plugin together.

