## Tool-routing quick reference

| Surface | Claude Code | GitHub Copilot | Codex |
|---|---|---|---|
| Skills install path | `.claude/skills/<name>/` | `.github/skills/<name>/` | `.agents/skills/<name>/` |
| Stop hook | `.claude/settings.json` | `.github/hooks/` | `.codex/hooks.json` (trust via `/hooks`) |
| Plan mode (interactive) | Yes | No (linear approval) | Yes (its own) |
| Multi-agent parallel | Yes (Agent tool) | Sequential | Native subagents, single-model |
| Workflow tool (ultracode) | Yes | No | No |

Copilot and Codex run the **prose** stages — the canonical source of truth.
The Workflow script is a Claude-only enhancement that mirrors them.

When in doubt: which tool's prompt did you type the slash into? That's
where the skill ran. There's no cross-tool dispatch.

